            <name>
                <baseName xml:lang="en">Uranium enrichment centrifuge plant</baseName>
            </name>
            <classificationInformation>
                <common:classification>
                    <common:class level="0" classId="e70d2ea9-becd-32e6-9944-c946e949f129">fuels</common:class>
                    <common:class level="1" classId="d9d22a1b-abde-33c5-a1bd-13c677d7ad0e">uranium</common:class>
                    <common:class level="2" classId="12eebfcf-f3b0-3e43-8621-e24a1b053a00">enriched</common:class>
                    <common:class level="3" classId="697dc0d1-c059-39d7-a044-f3060403e330">infrastructure</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The material and energy requirements for construction have been roughly estimated on the basis of the data from an old US reference and scaling them down by the ratio of the capacities (centrifuge process is modular, therefore in first approximation linearity can be assumed for requirements). It is assumed that 75% of reinforced concrete is dumped as non-contaminated waste from decommissioning. Although Russian facilities have higher capacity, the original dataset developed for URENCO plants has been directly used herewith for the previously explained reason, with the only difference of electricity requirements from the Russian mix. This mix has been approximated using existing ecoinvent v2.0 electricity datasets for Europe.;
UUID: eb105de6-e14c-3e73-9ff0-99f67a383c0b</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
